A fault hands the processor on but leaves the thread that made it ready,
so it is on no queue while another thread runs, and would run on at the instruction that faulted.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test smp-test qemu-replay
Report: thread runs with a fault to tell

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -876,7 +876,6 @@ void fault_dispatch(struct thread *t)
 {
     kputs("user fault\n");
     report_frame(&t->frame);
-    t->state = THREAD_STOPPED;
     t->flags |= THREAD_FAULTED;
     core_self()->trace_wake_bits = 0;
     struct notification *watch = thread_watch(t);
